## Generated contracts

These contract types are generated from the payload schemas the registry
pins, not written by hand:

{{ range .messages }}- `{{ .contract }}` from `{{ .schemaFile }}` (`{{ .message }}`)
{{ end }}
The schema documents are committed under `schemas/`, and `.intropy/messages.json`
records which message each one belongs to. Regenerate after a scaffold, or
after a pin moves:

```bash
pwsh ./generate-contracts.ps1
dotnet build
```

**The project does not compile until you run it.** That is deliberate: an
empty placeholder record would compile and then silently drop every payload
at run time, which is far harder to notice than a build error.

The generator and its type mapping live in `generate-contracts.ps1`, and
`ContractOptions.cs` is the single seam the components and the framework use
to reach its serialization settings. Both belong to the template library —
change them there to change how types are produced.

This preview generates one schema-backed contract per project; the script
refuses a second and says why.
{{- end }}
